full_article:
At least two people have died and 14 others are missing after an avalanche struck the base camp of a popular peak in the Himalayas, an association of Nepali mountain guides said on Sunday.

Police and expedition organizers said there were as many as 24 people in the area at the time of disaster.

Two bodies have been recovered from the area during the search, according to the Nepal National Mountain Guide Association (NNMGA), the only agency whose members are on the ground.

